  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a substantive denial that requires an appeal to overturn; resubmission is prohibited by the payer's duplicate claim rules. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is a valid and often effective next step to challenge the medical necessity of the bundling determination. The previous P2P request was likely premature or ineffective because it was made before the denial was formally adjudicated, so re-requesting it now with the denial on the table is the correct procedural move.",
